+/*
+ * Kernir patch 0015: read_toc parses the whole TOC, building an entry for
+ * every <file> and each entry's full pathname from its parent's, before
+ * the first header is returned, so the caller cannot stop a crafted TOC in
+ * time: a 14 KB xar of 4,000 nested folders cost 2.6 GB. While the TOC is
+ * parsed, an entry nested more than KERNIR_XAR_DEPTH levels deep, a
+ * pathname or link target over KERNIR_XAR_NAME_BYTES, and pathnames, link
+ * targets and hardlink target copies over KERNIR_XAR_NAMES_BYTES in all
+ * are refused (kernir_xar_refuse). These sit at or above what Kernir
+ * lists: 200 path components, 16 KiB per path, 64 KiB per name or link
+ * target and 256 MiB of names and link targets per archive (as in 0014).
+ */
